hadiths[10]{hadithnumber,text}:
"52","It is narrated from Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would kiss her while he was fasting."
"53","It is narrated from Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would kiss her while he was fasting."
"54","It is narrated from Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would kiss her while he was fasting."
"55","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to kiss her while he was fasting."
"56","Umm al-Mu'mineen Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: In the beginning, the obligatory prayer in residence and on a journey was two rak'ahs. Then, the prayer during travel remained two rak'ahs, while the prayer in residence was completed to four rak'ahs. Salih bin Kaysan said: I narrated this hadith to Umar bin Abdul Aziz (may Allah have mercy on him), so he asked: Did Urwah (may Allah have mercy on him) narrate to me that Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) used to perform four rak'ahs (complete prayer) during travel? Salih says: One day I saw Urwah (may Allah have mercy on him) with Umar bin Abdul Aziz (may Allah have mercy on him), so I asked him: How did you narrate that hadith on the authority of Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her)? So he narrated the hadith to me in the same way as he had narrated before. (Upon hearing this) Umar bin Abdul Aziz (may Allah have mercy on him) said to Urwah: You narrated to me that Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) used to perform four rak'ahs (complete obligatory prayer) during travel. Urwah (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Yes! That is how it is."
"57","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to pray at night while I would be lying on the bed in front of him. Ibn Abi Habibah said: In his narration, Khalid added the words ""lying like a corpse."" And when he intended to pray Witr, he would wake me up as well, and I would also pray Witr."
"58","Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: It was asked from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), ""A man has intercourse with his wife but does not ejaculate?"" So he said: ""He should perform ablution like the ablution for prayer and wash his private part."""
"59","Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: Jibreel (peace be upon him) came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) after the sun had declined and said: Stand up and lead the Zuhr prayer of four rak‘ahs. Then, when the shadow of everything became equal to its length, he came and said: Stand up and lead the Asr prayer of four rak‘ahs. Then, when the sun had set, he came and said: Stand up and perform the Maghrib prayer. Then, when the redness disappeared, he came and said: Stand up and lead the ‘Isha prayer of four rak‘ahs. Then he came when the dawn had become bright and said: Stand up and perform the Fajr prayer of two rak‘ahs. Then, on the next day, when the shadow of everything had become equal to its length, he came and said: Perform the Zuhr prayer of four rak‘ahs. Then, when the shadow of everything became twice its length, he came and said: Perform the Asr prayer of four rak‘ahs. Then he came at the same first time when the sun had set, and you performed the Maghrib prayer. Then, after the redness disappeared and it became quite dark, he came and led the ‘Isha prayer. Then he came when the dawn had become bright and led the Fajr prayer of two rak‘ahs. Then Jibreel (peace be upon him) said: The times of the prayers are between these two times."
"60","Ishaq bin Ibrahim narrated to us a hadith, he said, Ayub bin Sulaiman narrated to us a hadith, he said, Abu Bakr narrated to me from Salman bin Bilal, he from Yahya bin Saeed, he said Umar bin Abdul Aziz informed me similar to the previous hadith, except that in his narration he mentioned these words: Jibreel (peace be upon him) said: And these are the prayer (timings) for you and for the prophets before you."
"61","It is narrated from Abu Mas'ud Ansari and Bashir bin Abu Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with them both, and both were companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, that Jibreel, peace be upon him, came to the service of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and narrated a hadith similar to the previous hadith."
